<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jomo Kenyatta</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1897–<a href="/years/1978">1978</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jomo Kenyatta was a Kikuyu nationalist leader imprisoned by the British during the Mau Mau emergency. As leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kenya-african-national-union">Kenya African National Union</a> he became prime minister at independence on 12 December 1963 and president when Kenya became a republic in 1964. He ruled until his death in 1978, making Kenya effectively a one-party state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jomo-kenyatta.jpg" alt="Jomo Kenyatta" width="320" height="431" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pridan Moshe · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jomo_Kenyatta_(cropped)_in_June_15th,_1966.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
